# Written by `xbr new`. Game data, generated code, the toolchain and the
# bundles never enter git. The top-level entries are anchored (/x), and the
# ones a worktree holds as symlinks to the main checkout's are bare: a
# trailing-slash line matches a directory only.

# Your dump, and the analysis the pipeline writes beside it; `import`
# builds the dump beside it first and keeps the old one there until the
# new one is in place.
/Burnout 3 Takedown
/Burnout 3 Takedown.partial/
/Burnout 3 Takedown.old/

# Generated code and its key (`burnout3 package` regenerates when it differs).
/src/game/recomp/gen/
/src/game/recomp/gen.key.json
/src/game/recomp/.gen-regenerating

# The pipeline's intermediates.
/build/xr/

# Builds, and the packaging build trees (anchored: a change named
# openspec/changes/build-*/ is not one).
/build-win/
/build/
/build-*/
/build-logs/

# `burnout3 setup`: the pinned venvs, the toolchain, the toolkit and CLI clones.
/.venv*
/third_party
/external
/.xbr-pin
# `burnout3 package`'s stage records in a folder outside git (in a repo
# they live in the git directory).
/.xbr/

# `burnout3 package`: private bundles holding the game. Never commit them.
/dist/
*.dmg
*.exe
*.pdb
*.nsi
*.tar

# The bench host. Bare: a symlink to the workspace's one store.
bench-logs
/scripts/bench.env

# Game data, captures and game output, anywhere in the tree.
*.xbe
*.iso
*.xiso
*.xpr
*.xwb
*.adx
*.sfd
*.ipk
*.wav
*.bmp
*.png
# Screenshots of your own build for the README are the one exception.
!docs/images/*.png
*.ico
*.icns
*.ppm
*.raw
*.sav
*.xsv
UDATA/
TDATA/
saves/

*.pack
hud-pack.toml
*.xmv
*.rws
*.awd
CACHE/

# Work that belongs outside the repo: worktrees live in the workspace's
# wt/ (doctor still reports one here), A/B and probe output in its runs/.
/wt/
_local/
runs/

# Backups: a tracked game.toml.bak-<date> is how one gets in.
*.bak
*.bak-*

# Per-user agent settings.
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

*.log
__pycache__/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store

# --- this game ---
# Generated key files beside gen (gen.<n>/ from a split regenerate).
src/game/recomp/gen.*/

# Upstream's MSVC build (Setup.cmd, regen.sh) and its outputs.
build-xr/
out/
bin/
*.obj
*.dll
*.lib
*.exp
*.ilk
*.idb
setup.log
Play Burnout 3.cmd

# Upstream's screenshots are tracked (the export allows them while they
# equal upstream's).
!docs/screenshots/*.png

# The developer's own options (the game reads config/config.toml from the
# working directory over the build's config.default.toml).
config/config.toml

# Local-only agent and editor files.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.mcp.json
REPO_RULES.md
TESTING.md
.vs/
*.suo
*.user
.idea/
*.pyc
*.tmp
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
